~ start
Euthyphro: Indicted?
Socrates: Yes.
Euthyphro: You've been indicted, Socrates?
Socrates: It seems so.
Euthyphro: BY ZEUS!?
Socrates: By Zeus… 
Socrates: He calls himself Meletus.
Euthyphro: Now why would a young man such as himself be going after the very heart of our city?”
Socrates: He says I corrupt the youth, and disgrace our Gods.
Euthyphro: And the punishment?
Socrates: Public execution.
Euthyphro: Oh Gods! We must do something about this Socrates!
Socrates: I'll do what I've always done, young fellow.
Euthyphro: You've got a plan?
Socrates: I shall conduct moral philosophy, and in doing so, make that bastard Meletus ponder ethics for all of eternity. 
Socrates: Xaria is waiting for me, afterall!
=> END